> code and not anything that would be associated with the standard
> monster array(s)?

The Quest dialogue is all handled in questpgr.c.

> Essentially I'm looking for ways to communicate with the player at
> specific intervals and with non-randomized strings.  It appears that
> dialogue like the Oracle's (for example) would not be that difficult to
> replicate, but that dialogue is neither ordered nor long.

What you'd want is the com_pager() function that's used to deliver
non-role-specific text, not necessarily Quest-related; it's used for
the "legacy" message at gamestart, for example. Add an appropriately
numbered %Cc (or %Cp for short text) to the "General" section in
dat/quest.txt, then call com_pager(<that number>) when you want it
printed.

